he might have lost the election  but donald trump never went away  despite his poor record as president  multiple legal investigations and the  fact he tried to overturn the result in  2020 trump's grip on the republican  party seems to be strengthening  in august 2022 the republicans most  ardent trump critic liz cheney was  beaten by a trump endorsed candidate in  a republican primary election  could america be facing a second term  for president trump  i think he wants to be president again  absolutely i think he loved being  president and he would love to have the  legal protections of being president  again  he loves the politics he loves the  crowds he loves um he loves the fight he  feeds on it  and  um  and fundamentally i mean he loves the  attention and i think he's even more  likely to run now that um we've seen  this federal investigation get stepped  up in recent days  i think the deeper his legal jeopardy  the more likely it is that he will run  he'll be able to present himself as as a  victim  and run on the politics of grievance  more easily if he's if he's being  prosecuted he'll also  be able to  make the argument that  even more forcefully i think that these  um prosecutions are partisan  attempts to prevent him from returning  to the white house and so in that sense  running could help him with his legal  strategy uh at the same time that legal  problem could help him with his  political strategy there is a hard core  of the republican party that's desperate  for him to be the candidate and you see  their trump flags still flying  from their homes and from their boats  [Applause]  i don't think that if most republican  office holders  and even candidates around the country  were to speak uh  really candidly about it that most of  them  would want him to run again i think a  lot of the republican party is is ready  to to turn the page the just all the  craziness the distractions the even the  cult of personality itself  i think they're tired of it and there is  a um  another generation of of republican  candidates kind of waiting  impatiently in the wings but any of them  would have a very hard time overcoming  the advantage that donald trump begins  with critical primaries overnight in  wyoming and alaska with a crushing  defeat for liz cheney at the hands of  her trump-backed opponent liz cheney's  defeat didn't really come as a surprise  to anybody at least of all to her i  think she'd been expecting it  she has been the strongest voice  against him really within the republican  party it basically validates or  concretizes the idea that standing up to  donald trump spells electoral doom and i  think  liz cheney's loss will be  exhibit a  in the future for him of what happens if  you cross him the midterms are obviously  extremely important because a number of  candidates  are running particularly in senate races  in battleground states who are donald  trump's picks they were not  the party's picks and so in states where  the republicans have a real shot at  picking up a senate seat  they are now fighting kind of rearguard  action because the candidates that  they've put forward are so weak  so  if if the republicans are not able to  take the senate back as a consequence of  these essentially trump nominated  candidates  i think that will contribute to a real  sense of dissatisfaction with him with  him within the party now whether that  has any effect or not is  an entirely different question because  the reality is  donald trump's a proven loser as uh he  lost the presidency for his party he  lost the house and he lost the senate  for his party and other politicians in  the party were grinding their teeth  about this two years ago  and it hasn't stopped them from falling  into line once again now so even if uh  donald trump's chosen candidates  underperform that's not necessarily a  problem for him  when it comes to securing the republican  nomination again  i think he would struggle in a general  election  to win a majority of the votes that's  different than saying you can't be  elected president again though because  as we've seen there is a path to the  presidency that runs through  um piling up enough electoral votes and  key battleground states that could  potentially get them there again with  minority support the scariest  development in the last few years in  american politics has been the  denigration of  of the integrity of the vote republican  candidates for  key roles in counting the vote next time  around are people who have completely  bought into the so-called big lie that  that donald trump did win we may be in a  situation where  uh  he does well in these battleground  states and he has allies that he didn't  have last time in key positions  who were in a position to  falsify the results it's a dark  prospect  um  but i think we've learned you know in  the last few years that we have to take  these kinds of  scenarios very seriously because um  you know donald trump has repeatedly  broken through the boundaries of  everybody else's political imagination  if you'd like to read more of our  coverage of american politics please  click the link and please also subscribe  and thank you very much for watching  you

